The match is over.
Kasper, Sara, and I walk over to a bench.
We sit down, and we drink water.
"That was a really good game," Kasper says.
I smile and nod.
"Yes, I really like to play badminton," I answer.
Sara looks at me.
"What do you do in Copenhagen?" she asks.
"I work as a software engineer," I say.
"I come from Mexico, but I live here now."
"That sounds exciting," Sara says.
We drink the rest of our water.
"It is good to do sports in the winter," Kasper says.
I completely agree.
"Do you want to play with us again next week?" he asks.
"Yes, I would really like to do that," I answer.
"I promise to come back."
"Perfect, see you next Wednesday!" Sara says.
